{"step_index":65,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-24T07:44:35Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. 请接收数据获取蛋返回的上海温度结构化数据，将其渲染为友好的卡片 UI，突出展示上海当前温度及未来3天温度趋势。\n\n<summary>\n\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **Core request (user, Chinese):** As the 展示蛋 (e3) module, receive the structured Shanghai temperature data returned by the data-fetching egg (e2) and render it as a friendly card UI that highlights (a) Shanghai's current temperature and (b) a 3-day temperature trend.\n- **Success criteria:** A working card UI in the e3 workspace showing Shanghai's current temp prominently + a 3-day trend with per-day high/low and a visual trend indicator. All existing tests pass (backward compatibility).\n- **Constraints:** Source files ONLY under `/home/administator/workspace/create_idea/worktrees/e1/e3`; dependency-free plain Node (v24.21.0, `package.json` `\"type\": \"module\"`); keep the existing public API intact; no browser needed (module emits HTML strings); concise GitHub-markdown response with `file://` links.\n- **Ambiguity resolved:** e3 originally had no Shanghai data, so the canonical source is sibling egg e2's `shanghai_weather.json`, already copied into e3 as `data/shanghai.json` (self-contained & testable). e2's schema ≠ e3's card schema, so a normalization layer (`mapShanghaiData`) is required — not hand-editing sample.json, not hardcoding values.\n\n## 2. Progress\n**Verified complete (full files read + test run):**\n- `data/shanghai.json` (60 lines) present with full e2 schema (see §3).\n- `src/weather-card.js` (283 lines): doc comment, `WMO_CODE_MAP`, `WMO_ZH` (Chinese labels), `codeToCondition`, `round1`, `extractTime` (regex `/T(\\d{2}:\\d{2})/`), `WEEKDAY_ZH`, `weekdayOf` all written. Existing API intact: `unitOf`, `resolveCondition`, `themeFor`, `statRows`, `hourlyRow`, `renderWeatherCard`, `renderWeatherGrid`, `renderWeatherGridToElement`, `injectStyles`, `CARD_CSS`.\n- Ran `node test/weather-card.test.js` → **confirmed the bug** (see §3). Node v24.21.0.\n\n**In progress / incomplete:**\n1. `export function mapShanghaiData(raw)` NOT yet written.\n2. `dailyRow(daily, unit)` trend renderer NOT yet written; `.wc-daily` CSS NOT in `CARD_CSS`; `renderWeatherCard` NOT yet updated to include it.\n3. `index.html` still imports `data/sample.json` — needs to point at Shanghai.\n4. New tests for mapper + daily row NOT yet appended.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n**e2 schema (`data/shanghai.json`):**\n- `city:\"Shanghai\"`, `country:\"China\"`, `timezone:\"Asia/Shanghai\"`, `source:\"Open-Meteo API\"`.\n- `current_weather`: `observed_at:\"2026-10-24T15:15\"`, `temperature_c:20.7`, `feels_like_c:21.6`, `humidity_pct:87`, `wind_speed_mps:15.2`, `precipitation_mm:0.1`, `weather_code:51`.\n- `daily_forecast` (3 entries):\n  - `2026-10-24`: 中阵雨, code 81, max 20.9 / min 18.1, precip_prob 100\n  - `2026-10-25`: 毛毛雨, code 51, max 23.5 / min 17.9, precip_prob 54\n  - `2026-10-26`: 少云, code 2, max 22.8 / min 16.5, precip_prob 10\n\n**e3 card schema** (what `renderWeatherCard` expects): `{city, country, temp, unit, condition/icon, description, feelsLike, humidity, windKmh, windDirection, high, low, time, hourly, daily}`.\n\n**Conversion spec for `mapShanghaiData(raw)`:**\n- `city`←raw.city; `country`←raw.country.\n- `temp`←`current_weather.temperature_c` (20.7); `feelsLike`←`feels_like_c` (21.6); `humidity`←`humidity_pct` (87).\n- `windKmh`←`round1(wind_speed_mps*3.6)` (15.2→54.7).\n- `condition`←`codeToCondition(weather_code)?.code` (51→'drizzle'); `description`←`WMO_ZH[weather_code]` (51→'毛毛雨').\n- `time`←`extractTime(observed_at)`→\"15:15\".\n- `high`/`low`←`daily_forecast[0].temp_max_c`/`temp_min_c` (20.9/18.1).\n- `daily`←3 entries: `{date, label (今天/明天/weekday via weekdayOf), condition: codeToCondition(code)?.code, description: raw weather text, high, low}`.\n- Keep all existing exports unchanged.\n\n**Weekdays (verified):** 2026-10-24 = 五 (Fri), 2026-10-25 = 六 (Sat), 2026-10-26 = 日 (Sun). Labels: today=今天, tomorrow=明天, else weekday char.\n\n**CRITICAL BUG (root cause of test failure, confirmed by run):** `esc()` is broken — its declaration line is MISSING. Line 128 starts with a dangling `  return String(v ?? '').replace(...)` and line 131 has a stray `}`. Node error: `SyntaxError: Illegal return statement` at line 128. **Fix:** insert `function esc(v) {` before line 128. Clean single replacement: target the unique string `  return String(v ?? '').replace(/[&<>\"']/g, (ch) => ({` and prepend `function esc(v) {\\n`.\n\n## 4. Active Context\n- Working assumption: e2's `shanghai_weather.json` is canonical; already copied to e3 as `data/shanghai.json`.\n- Dependencies: `mapShanghaiData` needs `codeToCondition`/`WMO_ZH`/`weekdayOf` (all written). `dailyRow` needs `resolveCondition` (written).\n- `weekdayOf` uses `new Date(y, m-1, d)` — local-timezone aware, fine for these dates.\n- `CARD_CSS` is a const template literal at file end; `injectStyles()` reads it only at runtime, so const hoisting is safe.\n\n## 5. Next Steps (priority order)\n1. **Fix `esc()` bug** — insert `function esc(v) {` before line 128 of `src/weather-card.js`. (Prerequisite for everything else; module currently can't even parse.)\n2. **Add `export function mapShanghaiData(raw)`** — insert after `hourlyRow` (line 183) / before `renderWeatherCard` (line 185), per the conversion spec in §3.\n3. **Add `dailyRow(daily, unit)`** (internal) — renders a `.wc-daily` block: per day show label, condition icon (via `resolveCondition`), high/low, plus a visual trend indicator (▲/▼/→ arrow vs previous day's high + a CSS bar scaled by temp). Append `.wc-daily` CSS to `CARD_CSS` (insert before the closing `` `; `` on line 2